      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "side b",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>and honor their wives faithfully.\" And this (Miss) X listened to him (accepted the proposal)</li>\n<li>and willingly consented to be married to X b. Y, with the intention that she will</li>\n<li>serve, attend, esteem and honor him, in the manner of</li>\n<li>decent wives, the daughters of Israel, who esteem, honor,</li>\n<li>attend, and serve their husbands, faithfully, in purity</li>\n<li>and cleanness. Since this (miss) X has reached her majority, has attained puberty</li>\n<li>and is in her own jurisdiction, she willingly appointed for herself</li>\n<li>X b. Y, as her agent to receive her betrothal money</li>\n<li>from X b. Y, who sent by way of X b. Y, his messenger.</li>\n<li>And she consented to all that he does in her affair and stipulates on her behalf and as an obligation upon her.</li>\n<li>And two witnesses who are acquainted with her performed a qinyan with her for (affirming) this. The mohar</li>\n<li>which they fixed between themselves is so much. There remains incumbent upon him so much as delayed payment,</li>\n<li>(and) twenty-five zuz which are due her, and that which remains (as) the additional gift,</li>\n<li>a debt. And this is what this bride brought in from her paternal home: articles of</li>\n<li>gold worth so much, likewise articles of silver, likewise articles of copper,</li>\n<li>and likewise clothing. And X, the agent of X, undertook that</li>\n<li>the security for this marriage contract is undertaken by X, who sent him, and by</li>\n<li>his heir after him, against all the best (and) choice property, possessions and monies that he</li>\n<li>has under the heavens, indoors and outdoors, whether from real estate</li>\n<li>or movables, even from the shirt off his back.</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
      "schema:position": 2
    },
